  "independent_scope": "Whole native selected-source content on both mattes, all9 selected poses plus adopted neutral at inherited maximum body reference 430.000000px across5both-matte pages, and all7 decoded discrete recipe rows actually viewed. Historical unselected sheet cells are not accepted by viewing their whole source. Physical UI zoom/density and real-time/interpolated/MP4 output not measured.",
  "observations": [
    "Whole selected blink singleton and both four-pose split originals were actually inspected at native pixels on light and dark mattes. Round short ears with pink interiors, two oval white-surrounded brown eyes, six cheek lines, cream muzzle/belly, two rounded forepaws and two planted feet are clear; no extra limb, clipped fur/ear, broad alpha field or dirty paint seen.",
    "At inherited max body-reference430, fresh quiet blink keeps the neutral crown, chin, torso and feet close without nod/elongation. Other eight gestures preserve compact proportions; directional eyes and connected paws clearly present left/right, think/aha cheek poses and cheer are readable.",
    "Species A tilts head/short ears and B settles upright; modest ear/crown contour change is intentional active pose, without long rabbit ears or added tail. Native support/foot placement and common sheet scale remain visually coherent.",
    "All seven decoded static key-pose strips were actually viewed in both mattes; no missing limbs or abrupt disproportion apparent. This does not certify real-time playback or a completed MP4."
  ],
  "cautions": [
    "Mild hand-drawn crown/ear contour variation remains in active head/ear poses; physical UI zoom/density was not measured."
